.\" Made from the kstar help (src/help.rs); do not edit. See src/manual.rs.
.TH KSTAR-RUN 1 "" "Kleene Star" "Kleene Star Manual"
.SH NAME
kstar\-run \- run programs (files or folders of .kstar files)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBkstar run\fR [options] <files>...
\fBkstar\fR <file.kstar>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Runs each program. A folder means every .kstar file inside it, and
\fBkstar file.kstar\fR is short for \fBkstar run file.kstar\fR. With several files,
each file's output starts with its name, and a count of the files that
passed and failed comes at the end.
.PP
Imported files are checked before anything runs. A module's top level runs
the first time one of its names is used, without its print, test, draw and
trace statements.
.PP
The exit code is 0 when every program ran without errors and no test
failed, 1 otherwise, and 2 when the command itself was wrong.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<dir>\fR
where \fBdraw\fR writes its files (default: the current folder)
.TP
\fB\-\-allow-path\fR \fI<dir>\fR
let std.io also read and write files in <dir>; give it more than once for more folders. Without it a program may only use files in its own folder.
.TP
\fB\-\-fixed-clock\fR
std.benchmark reports every time as 0, so the output is the same on every run
.TP
\fB\-\-watch\fR
run again whenever a file changes; stop with Ctrl-C
.TP
\fB\-\-trace-calls\fR
print every function call with its arguments, and every return with its result
.TP
\fB\-\-eager-imports\fR
run each imported module at its import line, not when one of its names is first used
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<when>\fR
auto (the default), always or never. With auto, output is coloured only on a terminal and never when the NO_COLOR environment variable is set.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBkstar run examples/tour.kstar\fR
run one program
.TP
\fBkstar run labs/ \-\-out drawings\fR
run every program in labs/, writing drawings into drawings/
.TP
\fBkstar run \-\-watch lab1.kstar\fR
run lab1.kstar again on every save
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkstar\fR(1),
\fBkstar\-help\fR(1)
.PP
The reference and the tutorial: https://github.com/Pratham71/kleene\-star
